{
  "name": "RSS to LinkedIn drafts (approval queue)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## RSS to LinkedIn drafts (approval queue)\n\n**What it does**\nWatches an RSS feed (your blog, an industry site, a newsletter). For each new article it asks OpenAI to draft a LinkedIn post in your voice and adds it to a Google Sheet with status `pending review`.\n\n**It never posts anything.** You read the queue, edit the drafts you like, and post them yourself. That is on purpose: AI drafts are a starting point, and your name is on the post.\n\n**You need**\nOpenAI and Google Sheets credentials, and a `Drafts` tab with these headers: created_at, source_title, source_link, angle, draft, status, reviewer_notes\n\n**Setup**\n1. Put your feed URL in **New article in feed**.\n2. Describe your voice and audience in **Draft the LinkedIn post** (yellow note).\n3. Set your sheet ID in **Add to approval queue**, then activate.\n\nBuilt by AI Strike Force, aistrikeforce.com",
        "height": 700,
        "width": 580
      },
      "id": "37429c72-7db6-546c-a069-476879553626",
      "name": "RSS to LinkedIn drafts (approval queue)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -640,
        -100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Edit me\nPaste your RSS feed URL. It checks once an hour and only picks up items it has not seen.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 260,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "69292c25-83f5-519f-985f-adfd225d8bd4",
      "name": "Edit me: feed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Edit me: your voice\nReplace the bracketed parts of the system message with who you are, who you write for and two or three things you never say.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "affb6d89-cebc-59cf-b8f9-0c59c7b08cd9",
      "name": "Edit me: your voice",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        600,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "pollTimes": {
          "item": [
            {
              "mode": "everyHour"
            }
          ]
        },
        "feedUrl": "https://example.com/feed.xml"
      },
      "id": "4aa61495-0423-5131-9f82-44a580951e5a",
      "name": "New article in feed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.rssFeedReadTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "maxItems": 5
      },
      "id": "2338c14e-b61e-5f69-ae08-d6e3ec16e5c5",
      "name": "Max 5 per check",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.limit",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        220,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "6a907396-934c-573c-a313-9b27835b647f",
              "name": "title",
              "value": "={{ ($json.title || '').trim() }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "4f4707df-4945-5bbb-89e5-5c8171b272c5",
              "name": "link",
              "value": "={{ $json.link }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "2f24daef-6ecc-5030-bb94-a99db22bbfc4",
              "name": "summary",
              "value": "={{ String($json.contentSnippet || $json.content || $json.summary || '').replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim().slice(0, 2500) }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "2795ee3a-c40d-576e-8b16-866ee8d4c012",
              "name": "published",
              "value": "={{ $json.isoDate || $json.pubDate }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "bf41d9e5-9b2d-5882-90fe-66be424d4818",
      "name": "Clean up the article",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        440,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Article title: {{ $json.title }}\nLink: {{ $json.link }}\nArticle text (may be a summary):\n{{ $json.summary }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "You draft LinkedIn posts for [YOUR NAME], [YOUR ROLE] at [YOUR COMPANY]. Audience: [WHO YOU WRITE FOR, e.g. owners of small service businesses].\n\nWrite one post reacting to the article. Rules:\n- 120 to 200 words. Short paragraphs, one idea each.\n- First line is a plain, specific statement that makes the reader want the second line. No questions as hooks, no \"In today's fast-paced world\".\n- Add one practical takeaway or opinion of your own, not just a summary.\n- No hashtag walls (two at most, at the end), no emojis unless they replace a word, no em dashes.\n- Do not invent numbers, quotes or experiences. If the article gives a figure, cite it plainly.\n- End with the article link on its own line.\nAlso return \"angle\": a five word label of the point the post makes."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "id": "61d316e4-82a4-5bb0-98f0-fd9ae2c11bd8",
      "name": "Draft the LinkedIn post",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        660,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
